WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.280
Here are the results on the test years.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:07.938
Each bar is a model's RMSE divided by raw GARCH's RMSE on the same days.

00:00:08.388 --> 00:00:09.594
One means a tie.

00:00:10.044 --> 00:00:11.228
Below one is better.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.279
First, DWT.

00:00:13.729 --> 00:00:19.510
Its error ranges from about 5 percent lower for Nigeria to about 1 percent higher for IBM.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.780
Here decimation does not hurt.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.121
Now MODWT.

00:00:24.571 --> 00:00:27.180
Its bars sit almost exactly on the line.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.320
Zoom in.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:37.146
MODWT is slightly better on South Africa, Tunisia, Infosys and Google, and slightly worse on Nigeria and IBM.

00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:40.770
Every gap is about 1.3 percent or less.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:48.566
On the later stock years, 2015 to 2025, the differences remain tiny, and their signs change.

00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:53.728
So our honest reading: MODWT GARCH roughly matches raw GARCH.

00:00:54.178 --> 00:00:55.701
It does not clearly beat it.

00:00:56.151 --> 00:00:58.696
And the DWT version is slightly better.
